eai_type,handler_path
# Example override of the mapping table (section 6.3).
#
# To enable it: copy this file to `lookups/acl_endpoint_map_override.csv` in the
# installed app, then describe one mapping per line. The real file is NEVER shipped in
# the archive (D-5): an app upgrade therefore cannot overwrite it, since the archive
# does not contain it.
#
# It is loaded AFTER `bin/acl_endpoint_map.json` and overrides it: a key present in
# both takes the value from this file.
#
# `handler_path` must match the pattern ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._~-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9._~-]+)*$
# - a non-conforming line is discarded and traced in the diagnostic log, never used. No
# derivation heuristic is applied (section 6.2): a type absent from the table produces
# `acl_status=rejected`, `acl_error=unresolved_endpoint:<type>`.
#
# The two lines below are commented out: this example file must override nothing as it
# stands.
#an-unknown-type,data/ui/something
#another-type,admin/something-else
